counterCapture -- F-O40: UnitTests' counter OVERWRITES the grammar's digit set.

incant/unitTests:87 declares the test variable counter=0. Its name resolves (resolveName -> locate walks the search list)
to Grokking's counter=[0-9] (incant/grammar:29, used by Precision), and aCTionTraiT writes the value 0 into THAT node
(trait.setContent(TraiTdata), trait = the resolved node) before aCTionDefinE copies it into UnitTests. The copy shares the
body, so the grammar's rule now holds 0. Measured: with unitTests loaded Grokking["counter"] reads 0; without, the set.
Recon 17-20 carry the analysis; the R2 try-and-buy (branch om-r2-ownname, unmerged) showed that minting fresh at
aCTionDefinE does NOT fix it -- the write has already happened at TraiT time -- and that the fresh entry then loses its 0.

NEXT: RULED -- R2 is PARKED (SEQ 231 R1) as its own named item; candidate later home: the kant mirror of the define road.
