traitDataCapture -- aCTionTraiTdata writes a resolved VALUE in place.

A definition's value (DatA) resolves like any name. With a Modifier, aCTionTraiTdata writes the resolved node before
anything is copied: options.affiliation = isAttribute (always, on the ORIGINAL node, even when it then copies); and when
the node has no rStuff it runs setRuleStuff() and sets isRule = 1 on the ORIGINAL's body (a copy is made only when
rStuff already exists). Measured here: UnitTests' plain field maximus reads isRule 0 before  in another
registry and 1 after; the control rule NamE reads 1 throughout (the starred read is the one that discriminates).
Not the definition's own field (recon 20) -- the same capture on the value.

NEXT: BEST GUESS -- the value's writes belong to the value AS USED HERE: copy first, then write (the copy already exists
for the rStuff case; the affiliation write precedes it, and the no-rStuff arm writes the original). Grade: mechanism read
in the generated .mm, symptom measured. Promote by a build where the before/after lines above agree at 0; kill if a define
relies on promoting a foreign field to a rule through its value.

